.el .ds Aq '
.TH FATHOM_ANALYZE 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-analyze \- Print one episode\*(Aqs delta document — the model the TUI, the export and an agent all read
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom analyze\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-schema\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIEPISODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print one episode\*(Aqs delta document — the model the TUI, the export and an agent all read
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the delta document as JSON on stdout, and nothing else there
.TP
\fB\-\-schema\fR
Print `schemas/episode\-delta.schema.json`, the JSON Schema for the document, and stop
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Check the checked\-in schema against what this build generates; the CI form of `\-\-schema`
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
Write the generated schema to `schemas/`, replacing the checked\-in copy
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIEPISODE\fR]
The episode to analyse: an episode id, a commit, a rev (`HEAD~3`, `main`, `v1.2^{}`) or an oid prefix. Omitted with `\-\-schema`, which prints the contract instead of an answer
